comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T17:07:19.586Z",codex-root,"Keep this task open until code, tests, docs, and local/live verification are complete; only the executing parent plan remains in progress during initial implementation."
  "2026-08-06T17:31:08.961Z",codex-root,"Implementation adds three nested commands, one transport read-only boundary, current capability probing, normal automation-file reuse, and stable envelopes. Focused typecheck plus 99 tests passed before the full suite."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T17:07:19.586Z",codex-root,Use Home Assistant Core response shapes verbatim at the transport boundary and normalize only for deterministic CLI envelopes.
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T17:07:19.586Z",codex-root,test_condition can return template_errors alongside a boolean; subscribe_condition emits only changed result/error payloads once per second; execute_script returns context plus optional response.
  "2026-08-06T17:31:09.800Z",codex-root,Moving frame types and parsing into websocket-protocol.ts kept websocket.ts within the enforced 300-code-line ceiling without hiding behavior or weakening coverage.
